{"availability":"available","full":"tomzhu0225/simjecture","name":"simjecture","description":"Evidence-governed autonomous experimentation and falsification for computational science","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":10,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-15T08:34:19Z","updated":"2026-10-08T08:33:16Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["autonomous-science","computational-physics","falsification","hypothesis-testing","scientific-agents","simulation"],"demo":"https://simjecture.com/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T09:24:34.232Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T09:24:34.232Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T09:24:34.232Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T09:24:34.232Z","stars":10,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Simjecture is a research workspace for computational science. Work with an agent to turn a question into a bounded study, run experiments, search for counterexamples, and test repairs to failed hypotheses. The harness records what ran and requires independent review before a scientific claim can close.","Use a compatible API model or an installed native agent CLI. Start in the browser workspace; terminal and headless workflows are available when you need automation.","A recorded Gray–Scott study found a finite-domain counterexample. You can inspect its code, evidence and review without an API key or new simulations. Simulation results remain conditional on the model and numerical scope; see scientific limitations."],"features":["Investigate a question: work interactively, then launch a bounded autonomous","Challenge and repair hypotheses: search for counterexamples, preserve claim","Use scientific instruments: commission optional WarpX, operator-supplied","Continue an investigation: prepare a linked phase with a new budget and","Compare coding agents: run task-scoped benchmarks over recorded diagnostics"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tomzhu0225/simjecture/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2bce3d7097c24495ff5c8b017a8a3dca0f3abae289cf28740e723db6e23fd744","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T09:24:34.344Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T09:24:34.344Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Simjecture is a research workspace for computational science. Work with an agent to turn a question into a bounded study, run experiments, search for counterexamples, and test repairs to failed hypotheses. The harness records what ran and requires independent review before a scientific claim can close.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tomzhu0225/simjecture/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"optional","text":"It has a durable queue, separate visitor allowances, GitHub sign-in and an optional confined executor for general Python, solver inputs and application builds.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tomzhu0225/simjecture/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"2bce3d7097c24495ff5c8b017a8a3dca0f3abae289cf28740e723db6e23fd744","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tomzhu0225/simjecture/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T09:24:34.345Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T08:33:16Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tomzhu0225/simjecture/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T09:24:34.346Z","hash":"2bce3d7097c24495ff5c8b017a8a3dca0f3abae289cf28740e723db6e23fd744","originalBytes":8467,"storedBytes":8467,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["docs","how-to","research","workspace","agent","evidence","recorded","review","scientific","hosted","study","add","experiments","numerical","see","simjecture","archive","before","claim","demos","getting-started","independent","index.md","local","model","open","optional","question","release","service","ssh","terminal","api","benchmark","contributing.md","does","execution","files","follow","host","inspect","install","investigation","license","native","new","prepare","run","security.md","setup","